From 8f23cf465e748255694e1b4c824ae6c941f3b134 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Syco <syco@example.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 20:18:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add timelocked two-step admin transfer (fixes #870)

Replaces the instant, single-call set_admin with a propose -> timelock
-> accept flow so a compromised admin key can no longer hand over the
contract instantly and irreversibly.

- propose_admin_transfer(caller, new_admin, delay_secs): admin only,
  delay_secs must be >= MIN_ADMIN_TRANSFER_DELAY (1 day). Overwrites
  any existing pending proposal.
- accept_admin_transfer(caller): callable only by the proposed address,
  only once the timelock has elapsed.
- cancel_admin_transfer(caller): admin only, cancels a pending proposal.
- get_pending_admin_transfer(): view the pending proposal, if any.

The old set_admin entrypoint is removed entirely (not left in parallel)
so the timelock cannot be bypassed. Emits AdminTransferProposed /
AdminTransferAccepted / AdminTransferCancelled; acceptance also still
emits AdminChanged for existing indexers.

Tests cover accept-after-delay, accept-too-early rejection, cancellation,
wrong-acceptor rejection, non-admin propose/cancel rejection, and
below-minimum delay rejection.
